# Without this, `COPY . .` puts the local .env - Clerk secret key, model provider key - inside
# the image, where it survives every later layer and ships with the image to anyone who pulls
# it. Secrets reach the container at run time through env_file, never through the build.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Not secrets, just weight and staleness. node_modules is reinstalled inside the image for the
# right platform, and a host .next would be a build from a different environment.
node_modules
.next
out
build
dist

# Uploaded contracts belong to the host volume, not the image.
data
uploads

.git
.gitignore
.github

*.log
npm-debug.log*
coverage
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Tests and fixtures are not needed to run the server. The sample contracts are small and are
# kept, so a reviewer can try the app straight from the container.
tests
